<article class="env-lemma" id="0F1X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F1X">Lemma <span data-tag="0F1X">37.66.5</span>.</a> If $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Y \to Z$ are morphisms of schemes such that $g \circ f$ is ind-quasi-affine, then $f$ is ind-quasi-affine. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0F1U" data-tag="0F1U">37.66.2</a>, we may work Zariski locally on $Z$ and then on $Y$, so we lose no generality by assuming that $Z$, and then also $Y$, is affine. Then any quasi-compact open of $X$ is quasi-affine, so Lemma <a href="/tag/0F1U" data-tag="0F1U">37.66.2</a> gives the claim. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>